  "research_id": "fraud-payment-integrity",
  "title": "Fraud and Payment Integrity",
  "question": "Can one federal dollar be followed from appropriation through payment, State or NGO custody, downstream expenditure, correction and recovery?",
  "bluf": "Treasury has now confirmed two meetings of its cross-sector Payment Fraud and Scams Working Group, but the September 30 second-meeting post names no participants, agenda, charter, data-sharing instrument, deliverable or operating lineage. Its cited proof point is the separate September 9 Xinbi action: DOJ reports more than $52 million in cryptocurrency restrained while Treasury used OFAC authority to designate Xinbi and two supporting technology firms; restraint, seizure, blocking, forfeiture and victim return remain distinct. The operating administrative group is not shown to be the statutory task force proposed in H.R. 4936: the House Financial Services Committee approved the amended TRAPS bill 49-0 on September 16, but it was not enacted through the cutoff. Separately, the White House fraud task force remains a federated operating architecture: agencies own program screening and action, DOJ houses the National Fraud Enforcement Division and multi-agency National Fraud Detection Center, and State nodes consume or contribute leads and records. The September 22 CMS event supplies a completed agency-action receipt, but its expected $2.2 billion APTC return is not collected recovery and no NFDC lead/model lineage is published. Identity, eligibility, cancellation, restraint, blocking, forfeiture, expected recoupment, adjudication and collected recovery remain separate proof states.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-30",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The Treasury Payment Fraud and Scams Working Group delta is bounded to 2026-09-30 17:38 EDT; no second-meeting readout or partner-agency account had been located by then. The White House task-force operating-state answer is bounded to 2026-09-22; the agreement/AI return and Fraud Detection Constitution to 2026-09-14 17:44 EDT; and the NFDC Charter deep dive to 18:04 EDT. The core transaction-record thesis remains bounded to 2026-07-23, regional PA, Hawaii and Southeast lanes to 2026-07-31, and the Do Not Pay structural map to 2026-08-29. Refresh the second-meeting record, H.R. 4936 status, Charter publication, program, EO-output, agreement and case-attribution states before later present-tense use.",
  "use_note": "Use the September 30 Treasury working-group delta for the cross-sector payment-scam forum and the legal boundary between the operating administrative group and proposed TRAPS task force; use the September 22 update for the current White House task-force action state; the Charter deep dive for verified signatories and clause audit; the agreement/AI interlock for the Ohio specimen, PRAC bridge and Florida boundary; the governed Fraud Detection Constitution for the five-layer relationship map; and the vault transaction-record study for the maintained appropriation-to-recovery answer. Do not treat H.R. 4936 as enacted or the two task forces as legally identical; attribute Xinbi restraint, seizure and OFAC blocking to their actual actors; and do not convert restraint, blocking, estimates, referrals, stopped payments, charges, orders or aggregate rollups into forfeiture, victim return or collected recovery.",
